Package: tvrestoreR
Title: Unified, Flexible Package That Handles Both Denoising and Inpainting of Grayscale Images Under TV Regularization.
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Jay", "Lee", , "jaylee0717@tamu.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides tools for restoring corrupted images using total variation regularization. The package supports both inpainting (filling missing or masked pixels) and denoising. Users can supply an image and a mask of observed pixels, choose a regularization weight (lambda), and obtain a restored image that balances data fidelity and smoothness. This is particularly useful for image reconstruction tasks where preserving edges while smoothing noise or filling gaps is critical.
